Z||000006||stsmithgt||11-30-2000||09:42 AM||||When I bought my car, it didn't have a front plate and I don't think it ever had one installed.  I hope nobody enforces that law around here.  I would have to change my plates because I only have one.  I've seen some ugly mounting jobs on the front of some other GT's.  Don't want to have to deal with it.(DMV)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Master_Sushi||11-30-2000||03:32 PM||||My front plate "fell" "off" last weekend. So I patched the holes for it and put it in my trunk  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I couldnt be bothered to put it back on again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.||||reg||6
Z||000008||Standard||12-01-2000||01:42 AM||||My front plate holder.. uhhh.. broke somehow.. yeah that's it.  I stashed it in the trunk and keep my front plate in the bottom of the windsheild.  Looks so much better w/o it.  Haven't been pulled over for it yet, and I'm the one that usually get's pulled over for retarded stuff like that...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
